msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.abaqus_automation.BatchAbaqusProcessor.__init__:32 of
msgid ""
"Jobs are spread by :func:`~ABQflow.core.hosts.assign_hosts` in proportion"
" to each machine's ``weight``; when a machine has no explicit weight, its"
" concurrency capacity is used instead.  How many jobs each machine runs "
"*at once* is a separate knob, ``HostSpec.max_concurrent``, enforced "
"during execution — so a batch can send two concurrent jobs to one machine"
" and one to another.  Neither knob changes ``cpus=``: that is "
"``cpus_per_job``, per batch or per host, and nothing rewrites it."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.abaqus_automation.BatchAbaqusProcessor.__init__:41 of
msgid ""
"Core counts are measured, not assumed — a remote machine that leaves "
"``cpus_total`` unset is probed over SSH once, before any job is "
"dispatched.  As in a host-less batch, cores are advisory: asking for more"
" than a machine has is logged as oversubscription and then run anyway."
msgstr ""

