#: ../../../source/api/ABQflow.core.rst:39
msgid "ABQflow.core.hosts module"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts:1 of
msgid ""
"HostSpec — a machine that can execute Abaqus jobs, and how work is spread"
" over several."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts:3 of
msgid ""
"A batch with no host runs locally, exactly as it always has.  Supplying "
"one or more :class:`~ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec` objects is the only way"
" to reach the remote code path, so remote execution is strictly opt-in."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts:7 of
msgid ""
"Two independent knobs control multi-machine behaviour, and conflating "
"them is the mistake this module exists to prevent:"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts:10 of
msgid "``max_concurrent``"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts:11 of
msgid ""
"How many jobs may run on a machine **at the same time**.  A capacity "
"limit, enforced by a semaphore during execution."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts:14 of
msgid "``weight``"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts:15 of
msgid ""
"What **share of the batch** a machine should receive.  A throughput "
"preference, applied when jobs are assigned."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts:18 of
#, python-format
msgid ""
"They are not the same thing, and measurement showed why: of two machines "
"tested, the one with half the cores finished the same job 60% faster.  "
"Ranking purely by core count would have sent most of the work to the "
"slower machine. So ``weight`` defaults to ``max_concurrent`` (a "
"reasonable proxy) but can be set explicitly once you know how fast a "
"machine actually is."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.physical_cores:1 of
msgid "Physical core count of *this* machine, with a safe fallback."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.physical_cores:3 of
msgid ""
"``psutil`` is preferred; without it the count is of *logical* processors,"
" which over-estimates on an SMT machine.  Core count is only ever "
"advisory (licence tokens are the hard cap), so erring high is harmless."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.solver_tokens:3 of
msgid ""
"``ceil(5 * n ** 0.422)`` — re-exported from "
":mod:`~ABQflow.core.abaqus_automation` semantics so this module can be "
"read on its own.  Sublinear: 1→5, 2→7, 4→9, 8→13, 16→17 tokens, which "
"means widening a job costs far fewer tokens than running more jobs."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:1 of
msgid "A machine that can execute Abaqus jobs."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:5 of
msgid "name"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:6 of
msgid ""
"Short identifier used in logs, in per-host cache-marker filenames, and to"
" namespace fetched results.  Must be unique within a batch."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:8 of
msgid "hostname"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:9 of
msgid ""
"Hostname, or a **bare** IPv6/IPv4 literal — no square brackets, since "
"this goes straight to :func:`socket.getaddrinfo`.  A Windows link-local "
"address needs a *numeric* zone index (``fe80::1%12``), not an interface "
"name.  ``None`` designates the local machine."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:13 of
msgid "username, password"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:14 of
msgid ""
"Password authentication.  Prefer sourcing these from the environment; "
"never commit them."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:16 of
msgid "key_filename"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:17 of
msgid "Private-key path.  Takes precedence over *password* when set."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:18 of
msgid "port"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:19 of
msgid "SSH port."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:21 of
msgid ""
"**Absolute** path to ``abaqus.bat`` on this machine.  Empty means "
"\"inherit the batch default\", which is what a local host normally wants;"
" a remote host must set it, and the constructor refuses one that does "
"not."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:26 of
msgid ""
"A bare ``'abaqus'`` frequently fails under a non-interactive SSH session,"
" which inherits machine- and user-level environment but not whatever a "
"login shell profile adds — and installers often put Abaqus on the "
"installing user's PATH only.  Failing at construction beats discovering "
"it after the batch has been dispatched."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:31 of
msgid "work_root"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:32 of
msgid "Directory under which per-job working directories are created."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:34 of
msgid ""
"``cpus=`` for jobs sent here.  ``None`` inherits the batch default, which"
" is what keeps a homogeneous batch simple."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:36 of
msgid "cpus_total"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:37 of
msgid ""
"Physical cores.  Used to derive :meth:`capacity` when *max_concurrent* is"
" not given, and to report CPU oversubscription. ``None`` enables probe: "
"the local machine is read directly, and a remote machine is probed over "
"SSH once per batch "
"(:meth:`~ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.probe_cores`). "
"Setting it explicitly skips the probe."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:44 of
msgid ""
"Token budget for this machine.  A **hard** cap on concurrency — Abaqus "
"refuses to start a job it cannot license, whereas oversubscribing cores "
"merely slows things down."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:47 of
msgid "max_concurrent"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:48 of
msgid ""
"Explicit cap on simultaneous jobs here.  ``None`` derives one from cores "
"and tokens.  This is what lets a batch send, say, two jobs to one machine"
" and one to another."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:51 of
msgid "weight"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:52 of
msgid ""
"Share of the batch this machine should receive, relative to the others.  "
"``None`` falls back to :meth:`capacity`, so machines are fed in "
"proportion to how much they can run at once.  Set it explicitly when a "
"machine is faster per job than its core count suggests."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:58 of
msgid "Cores left free for the OS when deriving capacity."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:59 of
msgid "max_sessions"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:60 of
msgid ""
"Cap on concurrent SSH connections; keep below sshd's ``MaxSessions`` "
"(default 10), above which refusals look like random network errors."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:62 of
msgid "fetch_globs"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:-1 ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:-1
#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:-1
#: ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.run_hook:-1 of
msgid "tuple[str, ...]"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:63 of
msgid "Filename patterns pulled back after each phase."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:64 of
msgid "fetch_odb"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:65 of
msgid ""
"Also retrieve the ``.odb``.  Default ``False``: ODBs are frequently "
"multi-gigabyte and leaving them where the solver wrote them is the point "
"of running remotely."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:68 of
msgid "cleanup"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:69 of
msgid ""
"``'never'`` (default) | ``'on_success'`` | ``'always'``.  Defaults to "
"keeping everything, because a remote job whose directory was deleted "
"cannot be debugged."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:72 of
msgid "connect_timeout"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:-1 of
msgid "float"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:73 of
msgid "Seconds to wait for the SSH handshake."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:74 of
msgid "poll_interval"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:75 of
msgid ""
"Initial seconds between completion polls; backs off to "
"*poll_max_interval*."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:77 of
msgid "poll_max_interval"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec:78 of
msgid "Ceiling for the poll backoff."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec.local:1 of
msgid "This machine, as a pool member."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec.local:3 of
msgid ""
"Mixing it with remote hosts lets a batch use the submitting machine's "
"spare capacity alongside the others::"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec.local:11 of
msgid ""
"Everything a local host runs goes through :class:`LocalBackend`, so it "
"behaves exactly as a host-less batch does — no staging, no fetch, no SSH."
"  ``cpus_total`` is measured if not given."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec.is_remote:1 of
msgid "Whether this spec designates a machine reached over SSH."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec.shared_dir:1 of
msgid "Directory holding files reused across this machine's jobs."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec.shared_dir:3 of
msgid ""
"``*INCLUDE`` targets land here rather than in each job directory: a "
"shared mesh is often far larger than the deck that references it, and "
"uploading it once per job would make transfer, not solving, the dominant "
"cost of a batch.  Contents are content-addressed, so they survive between"
" batches and are never invalidated by a stale name."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec.shared_dir:9 of
msgid ""
"Not touched by ``cleanup``, which only ever removes job directories — "
"this is a cache, and keeping it is the whole point."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec.job_dir:1 of
