#: ../../../source/api/ABQflow.core.rst:46
msgid "ABQflow.core.inp\\_include module"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include:1 of
msgid ""
"Resolution of an INP file's ``*INCLUDE`` tree — shared by every INP-based"
" preparation."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include:4 of
msgid "Why this is one module rather than logic inside each strategy"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include:5 of
msgid ""
"``InpModifyStrategy`` and ``ExistingInpStrategy`` were solving two halves"
" of the same problem and neither half was complete: the first substituted"
" ``{{placeholder}}`` tokens but left ``*INCLUDE`` paths alone (so a "
"template written into the job directory pointed its relative includes at "
"the *job* directory, where they do not exist), the second rewrote "
"includes but rejected templates outright.  A deck that is both "
"parameterised *and* modular — the common shape for a scenario file that "
"includes a shared mesh and a material fragment — could not be expressed "
"at all."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include:14 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Resolving the whole tree in one place makes ``existing_inp`` simply the "
"``params={}`` case of ``inp_based``, and gives the two strategies the "
"same behaviour on nested includes for free."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include:19 of
msgid "The two tiers"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include:20 of
msgid "Every file in the tree is classified once:"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include:22 of
msgid ""
"**parameterised** — it contains ``{{...}}`` of its own, *or* one of its "
"descendants does.  The descendant clause matters: if a static fragment "
"includes a parameterised one, the fragment's own ``*INCLUDE`` line has to"
" be rewritten to point at the per-job copy, so the fragment cannot be "
"shared either.  Parameterised files are substituted and written into the "
"job directory, and the directive naming them becomes a **bare filename** "
"(Abaqus resolves those against the job's working directory)."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include:30 of
msgid ""
"**static** — everything else, typically the large mesh or geometry that "
"is identical across the batch.  The file is left alone on disk and the "
"directive naming it becomes its **local absolute path**, so the deck "
"resolves from any working directory."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include:35 of
msgid ""
"That split is deliberately readable back off the deck: after resolution a"
" bare filename *means* \"per-job file, sitting in the job directory\" and"
" an absolute path *means* \"shared file that N jobs point at\".  Remote "
"staging can therefore decide where each target belongs by looking at the "
"deck alone, without a manifest threaded through from preparation."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.IncludeResolutionError:1 of
msgid "Bases: :py:class:`Exception`"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.IncludeResolutionError:1 of
msgid "An ``*INCLUDE`` tree could not be resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.IncludeResolutionError:3 of
msgid ""
"Raised for a target that does not exist on disk, a file that cannot be "
"read, or a cycle.  Carries the referencing file and the path the "
"directive resolved to, because \"file not found\" without both of those "
"is nearly useless when includes nest."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.read_inp_text:1 of
msgid "Read an INP file without depending on the machine's locale."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.read_inp_text:3 of
msgid ""
"Python's text mode defaults to the system encoding — GBK on a Chinese "
"Windows, cp1252 elsewhere — so a plain ``open(path)`` raises on any deck "
"those codecs reject.  A UTF-8 byte-order mark is enough to trigger it, "
"which makes decks exported by many editors unreadable on exactly the "
"machines this package targets."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.read_inp_text:9 of
msgid ""
"Decoding order: UTF-8 (BOM stripped if present), then latin-1, which "
"never fails and preserves the bytes.  Abaqus keywords are ASCII either "
"way, so the fallback only affects comments and free-text fields."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.write_inp_text:1 of
msgid "Write INP text as UTF-8, leaving line endings exactly as given."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:1 of
msgid "Outcome of walking one ``*INCLUDE`` tree — text only, nothing written."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:3 of
msgid ""
"Keeping the writes in the caller means a tree that fails validation (an "
"uncovered placeholder, a missing ``*STEP``) leaves no half-built job "
"directory behind."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:9 of
msgid "root_text"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:10 of
msgid ""
"The root deck, includes rewritten and placeholders substituted, ready to "
"be written to ``ctx.inp_path``."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:12 of
msgid "materialized"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:13 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``{filename: content}`` for every parameterised include.  Each must be "
"written into the job directory under exactly that filename — the "
"rewritten directives name them without a path."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:16 of
msgid "shared"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:17 of
msgid ""
"Absolute local paths of the static includes the tree points at, in first-"
"seen order.  Informational here; remote staging re-derives the same set "
"from the deck."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:20 of
msgid "placeholders"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:-1 of
msgid "frozenset[str]"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:21 of
msgid ""
"Every ``{{name}}`` seen anywhere in the tree, so the caller can check "
"parameter coverage across all files rather than only the root."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:23 of
msgid "has_step"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.ResolvedInp:24 of
msgid "Whether any file in the tree contains a ``*STEP`` keyword."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_target:1 of
msgid "Resolve one raw ``INPUT=`` value against the file that referenced it."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_target:3 of
msgid ""
"Relative targets are resolved against the *referencing file's* directory,"
" which is what Abaqus does and what makes a directory of scenario decks "
"portable.  Separators are normalised both ways: decks are routinely "
"authored on one platform and run on another, and Abaqus accepts either."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:1 of
msgid "Walk *root_path*'s include tree, substituting params and rewriting paths."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:5 of
msgid "root_path"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:6 of
msgid ""
"The deck to resolve.  Always treated as per-job: its text comes back in "
":attr:`ResolvedInp.root_text` rather than in ``materialized``."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:8
#: ABQflow.core.spec.PreparationSpec:39
#: ABQflow.core.strategies.InpModifyStrategy:11
#: ABQflow.core.strategies.InpPreparationStrategy:26
#: ABQflow.core.strategies.MonolithicWorkflowStrategy:12 of
msgid "params"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:-1 of
msgid "dict, optional"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:9 of
msgid ""
"``{{placeholder}}`` substitutions, applied to every file in the tree. A "
"placeholder with no matching key is left **untouched** rather than "
"raising, so the caller can report the full set of missing parameters at "
"once instead of failing on the first one."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:13 of
msgid "reserved_names"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:14 of
msgid ""
"Filenames already spoken for in the job directory (at minimum the job's "
"own ``<job_name>.inp``).  A parameterised include whose basename collides"
" with one of these — or with another include already placed — is renamed "
"with a short digest of its source path rather than overwriting it."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:19 of
msgid "follow_includes"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:20 of
msgid ""
"If ``False``, the root is substituted but its ``*INCLUDE`` lines are left"
" exactly as written.  Escape hatch for decks whose includes are resolved "
"by something outside ABQflow."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:-1 of
msgid "logging.Logger, optional"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:24 of
msgid "Progress destination; a module logger is used if omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:28 of
msgid "ResolvedInp"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:29 of
msgid "Text to write, plus what the caller needs to validate it."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:33 of
msgid "IncludeResolutionError"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.inp_include.resolve_include_tree:34 of
