#: ../../../source/api/ABQflow.core.rst:60
msgid "ABQflow.core.remote\\_launch module"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch:1 of
msgid "Pure builders for detached remote execution — no I/O, no network."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch:3 of
msgid ""
"Kept separate from the SSH backend so every decision here is unit-"
"testable with plain strings, in the same spirit as "
":meth:`AbaqusRunner.build_solver_command`."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch:8 of
msgid "Why the solver must be detached at all"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch:9 of
msgid ""
"Holding an SSH channel open for the duration of a solve makes the job as "
"fragile as the connection: a laptop sleeping, a Wi-Fi roam, a VPN "
"reconnect or sshd's ``ClientAliveInterval`` closes the channel, and "
"Windows OpenSSH terminates the session's process tree with it.  A six-"
"hour job dies at hour four.  So the solver is launched detached and "
"progress is read from files on the remote disk, which makes the poll loop"
" stateless: it can lose the connection, reconnect, and resume with "
"nothing lost."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch:17 of
msgid ""
"Measured on the target machines (2026-08-30): ``Win32_Process.Create`` "
"survives channel close and reports a usable PID.  ``schtasks`` was "
"rejected outright, and ``start /b`` returned success and then never ran "
"the batch file at all — a *silent* failure, which is why the launcher is "
"verified by looking for output rather than by trusting a return code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../docstring ABQflow.core.remote_launch.WORKDIR_FAILED_RC:1 of
msgid ""
"Return code the launcher writes when it cannot enter the working "
"directory. Deliberately outside the range Abaqus itself uses, so the "
"sentinel says *which* failure happened rather than just \"non-zero\"."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.find_includes:1 of
msgid "Return the raw ``INPUT=`` paths of every ``*INCLUDE`` in *text*."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.rewrite_includes:1 of
msgid "Rewrite every ``*INCLUDE, INPUT=`` path through *resolver*."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.rewrite_includes:3 of
msgid ""
"``ExistingInpStrategy`` deliberately rewrites includes to **local "
"absolute paths**, which are guaranteed not to exist on another machine — "
"so every job with an include would fail remotely with a cryptic Abaqus "
"preprocessing error.  This is the substitution step that fixes that; the "
"caller decides *what* each path becomes."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.rewrite_includes:9 of
msgid ""
"Kept free of I/O on purpose: the caller resolves and uploads first, then "
"hands in a finished mapping, so this stays a pure function that a unit "
"test can drive with plain strings."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.rewrite_includes:15
#: ABQflow.core.runner.extract_json:12 of
msgid "text"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.rewrite_includes:16 of
msgid "INP contents."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.rewrite_includes:17 of
msgid "resolver"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.rewrite_includes:18 of
msgid ""
"``(original_path) -> str or None``.  ``None`` leaves that directive "
"untouched, which is what an unresolvable path should do — silently "
"rewriting it to something that does not exist would be worse."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.rewrite_includes:25 of
msgid "The rewritten deck."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.build_launcher_bat:1 of
msgid ""
"Render the ``.bat`` wrapper that runs the solver and writes the rc "
"sentinel."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.build_launcher_bat:3 of
#, python-format
msgid ""
"``interactive`` is kept deliberately: it is what makes ``abaqus.bat`` "
"block, so ``%ERRORLEVEL%`` refers to the solver and not to the launcher."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.build_launcher_bat:7 of
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The parentheses around the final ``echo`` are load-bearing. ``echo "
"%ERRORLEVEL%> file`` expands to ``echo 0> file``, and cmd.exe reads a "
"digit immediately before ``>`` as a **file-descriptor number** — so it "
"redirects stdin and the sentinel ends up with no return code in it.  "
"Wrapping the echo in a command block keeps any digit away from the "
"redirection operator.  This was observed in practice, not theory."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.build_detach_script:1 of
msgid "Render the PowerShell that launches *bat_path* detached."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.build_detach_script:3 of
msgid ""
"``Win32_Process.Create`` re-parents the new process to ``WmiPrvSE.exe`` "
"rather than the sshd session, so closing the SSH channel cannot reap it, "
"and it returns the real PID that the terminate ladder needs."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.parse_detach_output:1 of
msgid "Parse ``(ReturnValue, ProcessId)`` from the launcher's output."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.parse_detach_output:3 of
msgid "``ReturnValue`` 0 means the process was created."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.parse_rc_sentinel:1 of
msgid "Extract the solver return code from ``<job>.abqflow.rc`` contents."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.poll_verdict:1 of
msgid "Classify one poll tick as ``'running'`` / ``'finished'`` / ``'timeout'``."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.poll_verdict:3 of
msgid ""
"The rc sentinel is the only authoritative completion signal.  ``.lck`` "
"absence never means finished on its own: Abaqus does not create it for "
"the first few seconds after launch (measured: still absent at t=2 s, "
"present at t=5 s), so treating \"no lck\" as \"done\" reports success "
"before the solver has started."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.grace_period:1 of
msgid "G = clamp(0.05 x T, 30, 300) seconds — same formula as the local ladder."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.quote_arg:1 of
msgid "Quote *arg* for a Windows command line if it needs it."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.build_cmd_line:1 of
msgid "Join *argv* into a single Windows command line."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.wrap_cmd:1 of
msgid "Wrap *argv* as ``cmd /s /c \"…\"`` — shell-agnostic and quote-safe."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.wrap_cmd:3 of
msgid ""
"``/s`` gives cmd's one well-defined quoting rule: strip exactly the first"
" and last quote character and treat the rest literally.  Wrapping "
"explicitly means the command works whether sshd's default shell is "
"``cmd.exe`` or PowerShell, without touching the ``DefaultShell`` registry"
" key on the target."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.wrap_powershell:1 of
msgid "Wrap a PowerShell *script* as a quote-free ``-EncodedCommand`` call."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.remote_launch.wrap_powershell:3 of
msgid ""
"Base64-of-UTF-16LE carries no quotes at all, so the command line survives"
" any intermediate shell untouched — this removes an entire class of "
"Windows quoting bugs rather than trying to escape around them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/ABQflow.core.rst:67
msgid "ABQflow.core.runner module"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner:1 of
msgid ""
"AbaqusRunner — subprocess gateway that encapsulates every shell call a "
"strategy needs."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner:3 of
msgid ""
"Provides environment detection (abqpy / CAE kernel / odbAccess), "
"sentinel-based JSON extraction, timeout-safe command execution, solver "
"diagnostics, and a ``record_only`` dry-run mode."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.compile_failure_marker:1 of
msgid "First failure marker present in *stdout*/*stderr*, or ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.compile_failure_marker:3 of
msgid ""
"Used to second-guess a zero exit code from ``abaqus make``.  Returning "
"the marker rather than a bool lets the caller say *why* it overrode the "
"rc."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.Timeouts:1 of
msgid "Per-stage time limits."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.Timeouts:3 of
msgid ""
"These were once a single number applied to five very different things — "
"the solver wait, preflight, subroutine compilation, hook scripts and "
"every other command.  That coupling made the obvious response to a long "
"solve (\"raise the timeout\") also hand a hung hook script the same many-"
" hour budget, so the stages are separated here."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.Timeouts:9 of
msgid ""
"``solver`` defaults to ``None`` — no wall-clock cap at all.  That is safe"
" because completion is no longer decided by elapsed time: the poll loop "
"watches the rc sentinel *and* process liveness, so a job that dies is "
"caught within a poll interval while one that is genuinely still solving "
"is left alone.  A solve is worth waiting for; a hung hook is not, which "
"is why the short stages keep finite defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.Timeouts:18 ABQflow.core.spec.SubroutineSpec:10 of
msgid "solver"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.Timeouts:19 of
msgid "Wall-clock cap on the solver run.  ``None`` means none."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.Timeouts:20 ABQflow.core.spec.JobSpec:16 of
msgid "preflight"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.Timeouts:21 of
msgid ""
"Cap on ``syntaxcheck`` / ``datacheck``.  Generous, because preprocessing "
"a large deck legitimately takes minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.Timeouts:23 of
msgid "compile"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.Timeouts:24 of
msgid "Cap on ``abaqus make``."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.Timeouts:25 of
msgid "hook"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.Timeouts:26 of
msgid ""
"Cap on extraction hooks and any other command routed through "
":meth:`AbaqusRunner._run`."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.Timeouts.coerce:1 of
msgid "Build a :class:`Timeouts` from a scalar, a mapping, or itself."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.Timeouts.coerce:3 of
msgid ""
"A bare number keeps the historical meaning — the same limit everywhere — "
"so existing callers passing ``timeout=3600`` behave exactly as before.  "
"``None`` selects the per-stage defaults above."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.CommandRecord:1 of
msgid "One command that was (or would be) executed."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.extract_json:1 of
msgid "Extract a JSON object from subprocess stdout."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.extract_json:3 of
msgid ""
"Protocol: the script wraps its JSON payload between sentinel markers "
"``===ABQ_RESULT_BEGIN===`` and ``===ABQ_RESULT_END===``.  Only that form "
"is accepted — Abaqus prints a banner before user code runs and hooks are "
"free to print whatever they like, so guessing at an unmarked payload "
"picks up whichever brace happens to come last.  :mod:`ABQflow.hookkit` "
"emits the markers for you."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.extract_json:13 of
msgid "Raw stdout captured from a subprocess call."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.extract_json:18 of
msgid "Parsed JSON payload."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.extract_json:23 of
msgid "If the sentinel markers are absent, or the payload is not valid JSON."
msgstr ""

