msgid "Whether this runner executes on another machine."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.artifact_exists:1 of
msgid "Whether *local_path*'s twin exists on the **executing** machine."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.artifact_exists:3 of
msgid ""
"Strategies guard on artifacts with plain ``os.path.exists``, which is "
"correct locally but wrong once the solver runs elsewhere: the ``.odb`` "
"only ever exists on the remote machine, so a local check would make every"
" remote extraction silently return all-``None``.  Pass the *local* path "
"here and the runner maps it for you."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.local_backend:1 of
msgid "A backend that always runs on **this** machine."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.local_backend:3 of
msgid ""
"Preparation happens locally by design — the INP is built here and then "
"shipped — so preparation commands must not be routed to the remote "
"backend, whose ``abaqus_exe`` and paths belong to a different machine."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.stage_inputs:1 of
msgid "Upload everything the solver needs onto the executing machine."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.stage_inputs:3 of
msgid ""
"Handles the ``*INCLUDE`` problem found during the remote spike: the "
"directives point at local paths that cannot exist on the far side, so any"
" deck with an include fails remotely with an opaque preprocessing error."
"  The whole tree is walked — see :meth:`_rewrite_deck` — and each target "
"is placed by tier: per-job files travel with the job, static ones land in"
" the machine's shared directory, once per machine rather than once per "
"job.  See :meth:`_stage_include`."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.stage_inputs:13 of
msgid "bool or None"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.stage_inputs:14 of
msgid ""
"``None`` when running locally (nothing to do), otherwise whether staging "
"succeeded."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.fetch_results:1 of
msgid "Copy the executing machine's small artifacts into the local job dir."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.fetch_results:3 of
msgid ""
"This is what lets :func:`~ABQflow.core.diagnostics.diagnose` stay "
"completely unchanged: ``.sta`` / ``.msg`` / ``.dat`` are kilobytes to "
"megabytes and come back, while the multi-gigabyte ``.odb`` stays put. A "
"no-op when running locally."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.build_script_command:1 of
