#: ABQflow.core.strategies.InpPreparationStrategy:3 of
msgid ""
"One pipeline serves both use cases, because they are the same pipeline "
"with a different amount of work in the first step::"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.InpPreparationStrategy:8 of
msgid ""
"*substitute* walks the ``*INCLUDE`` tree once, replacing "
"``{{placeholder}}`` tokens and rewriting every directive (see "
":mod:`ABQflow.core.inp_include` for the per-file rules).  With ``params``"
" empty there is simply nothing to substitute, which is exactly the \"pre-"
"existing INP\" case — it is not a separate strategy, just this one with "
"an empty parameter set."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.InpPreparationStrategy:14 of
msgid ""
"*validate* checks the resolved tree, never the root alone: a modular deck"
" legitimately keeps its ``*STEP`` — or a ``{{placeholder}}`` — in an "
"included fragment, so a root-only check gives the wrong answer on exactly"
" the decks this class exists to support."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.InpPreparationStrategy:19 of
msgid ""
"*stage* writes the result into the job directory.  Nothing is written "
"until validation passes, so a rejected deck leaves no half-built job "
"behind."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.InpPreparationStrategy:25 of
msgid "Template or finished INP to prepare."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.InpPreparationStrategy:27 of
