msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ExistingInpStrategy:1 of
msgid ""
"Preset of :class:`InpPreparationStrategy` that asserts the deck is "
"finished."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ExistingInpStrategy:3 of
msgid ""
"Backs ``kind='existing_inp'``, the UC-03 \"pre-existing INP batch\" case."
" Mechanically it is the parent with an empty parameter set; what it adds "
"is an *assertion*: a ``{{placeholder}}`` anywhere in the tree is reported"
" as \"you handed a template to a batch of finished decks\", which is the "
"mistake actually being made, rather than as a missing parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ExistingInpStrategy:12 of
msgid "Absolute or relative path to the existing INP file."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ExistingInpStrategy:14 of
msgid ""
"If ``True`` (default), rewrite ``*INCLUDE, INPUT=rel_path`` to use "
"absolute paths resolved against the referencing file's directory."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ExistingInpStrategy:17 of
msgid ""
"See :class:`InpPreparationStrategy`.  Replaces the old ``staging_mode``, "
"which asked a per-job question that no longer has one answer."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.SubroutineCompileStrategy:1 of
msgid "Compiles a user subroutine via ``abaqus make`` before preparation."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.SubroutineCompileStrategy:3 of
msgid ""
"Not part of the :class:`PreparationStrategy`/:class:`ExtractionStrategy` "
"ABC hierarchies — compilation is its own concern with a single "
"implementation today (YAGNI; add a registry like "
":data:`~ABQflow.core.registry.PREPARATION_REGISTRY` if multiple compile "
"backends are ever needed)."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.SubroutineCompileStrategy:13 of
msgid "cache"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.SubroutineCompileStrategy:14 of
msgid ""
"If ``True`` (default), skip recompilation when the source file's content "
"hash matches the last successful compile (see "
":meth:`~ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.subroutine_needs_recompile`)."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.SubroutineCompileStrategy.compile:1 of
msgid "Compile the subroutine, or skip if precompiled/cached."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.SubroutineCompileStrategy.compile:5 of
msgid "tuple[bool, str]"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.SubroutineCompileStrategy.compile:6 of
msgid ""
"``(success, message)`` — *message* is empty on success (or a skip note), "
"or the compiler's raw stdout+stderr on failure. No regex parsing of "
"compiler errors is performed (see "
":meth:`~ABQflow.core.runner.AbaqusRunner.run_compile`)."
msgstr ""

