msgid "List of hook descriptors, each with ``script_path`` and ``tasks``."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.DatExtractionStrategy:1 of
msgid "Extract results from the ``.dat`` file via hook scripts."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.DatExtractionStrategy:3 of
msgid ""
"An ODB is often too large to open just to read a few numbers; adding "
"``*NODE PRINT`` / ``*EL PRINT`` to the deck makes Abaqus write the same "
"values as text into ``<job>.dat``, and this strategy reads them back."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.DatExtractionStrategy:7 of
msgid ""
"Runs the hook under the **host** Python, not ``abaqus python``: a "
"``.dat`` is plain text, so parsing it needs neither the Abaqus kernel nor"
" a license token — which is most of the point.  With a remote backend the"
" file is fetched into the local job directory first and the hook then "
"runs here; shipping a text parser to the solver machine would buy nothing"
" and would leave sidecar CSVs on the wrong host."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.DatExtractionStrategy:14 of
msgid ""
"Each hook script receives ``--dat_path`` as a common argument and a JSON "
"task list via ``--tasks_json``.  ``datkit.py`` is staged alongside "
"``hookkit.py`` so hooks can ``import datkit``."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModelPropertiesExtractionStrategy:1 of
msgid "Extract material/property data from the INP *before* simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModelPropertiesExtractionStrategy:3 of
msgid ""
"Runs in the CAE kernel environment (``abaqus cae noGUI``) because it "
"needs ``mdb`` access.  Each hook script receives ``--inp_path`` as a "
"common argument and a JSON task list via ``--tasks_json``."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.JobWorkflowStrategy:1 of
msgid "Interface for a complete job workflow."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.JobWorkflowStrategy:5 of
msgid "MonolithicWorkflowStrategy"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.JobWorkflowStrategy:6 of
msgid "Single-script workflow that handles everything itself."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.JobWorkflowStrategy:7 of
msgid "ModularWorkflowStrategy"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.JobWorkflowStrategy:8 of
msgid ""
"Multi-phase pipeline: optional subroutine compile, preparation, optional "
"preflight, pre-extraction, simulation, post-extraction."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.JobWorkflowStrategy:12 of
msgid "Optional phase-separated protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.JobWorkflowStrategy:13 of
msgid ""
"Subclasses *may* additionally implement ``prepare_only(ctx, runner, "
"logger, status_manager=None) -> tuple[dict, JobStatusManager]``, "
"``simulate_only(...) -> tuple[dict, JobStatusManager, bool]`` (the "
"``bool`` signals whether the pipeline should stop), and "
"``extract_only(...) -> tuple[dict, JobStatusManager]`` so that "
":class:`~ABQflow.core.abaqus_automation.AbaqusCalculation` can invoke a "
"single phase (see its ``execute(phase=...)`` parameter). This is not "
"required by the ABC — :class:`MonolithicWorkflowStrategy` and user-"
"defined strategies that don't implement it simply raise "
"``NotImplementedError`` when a phase-only call is attempted."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.JobWorkflowStrategy.execute:1
#: ABQflow.core.strategies.MonolithicWorkflowStrategy.execute:1 of
msgid "Run the full workflow and return a result dict."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.JobWorkflowStrategy.execute:6
#: ABQflow.core.strategies.MonolithicWorkflowStrategy.execute:6 of
msgid "Job context."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.JobWorkflowStrategy.execute:8
#: ABQflow.core.strategies.MonolithicWorkflowStrategy.execute:8 of
msgid "Subprocess runner for all subprocess calls."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.JobWorkflowStrategy.execute:15
#: ABQflow.core.strategies.MonolithicWorkflowStrategy.execute:15 of
msgid ""
"Must contain at least a ``'status'`` key (a :class:`JobStatus` or its "
"string value).  May include extracted results."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy:1
#: ABQflow.core.strategies.MonolithicWorkflowStrategy:1 of
msgid "Bases: :py:class:`~ABQflow.core.strategies.JobWorkflowStrategy`"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.MonolithicWorkflowStrategy:1 of
msgid "Single-script workflow: one script does everything."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.MonolithicWorkflowStrategy:3 of
msgid ""
"The script is launched via the CAE kernel (``abaqus cae noGUI``) and must"
" print its JSON results wrapped in the sentinel markers "
"``===ABQ_RESULT_BEGIN===`` / ``===ABQ_RESULT_END===``.  The result dict "
"is expected to contain at least a ``'status'`` key."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.MonolithicWorkflowStrategy:11 of
msgid "Path to the monolithic script."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.MonolithicWorkflowStrategy:13 of
msgid "Key-value parameters forwarded as ``--key value`` CLI arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy:1 of
msgid ""
"Multi-phase pipeline: [compile], preparation, [preflight], pre-"
"extraction, simulation, post-extraction."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy:3 of
msgid ""
"Uses a :class:`JobStatusManager` internally to track the job through each"
" phase.  If any phase fails the pipeline stops and returns the terminal "
"status immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy:7 of
msgid ""
"``execute()`` composes three independently callable phase methods — "
":meth:`prepare_only`, :meth:`simulate_only`, :meth:`extract_only` — so "
"that :class:`~ABQflow.core.abaqus_automation.AbaqusCalculation` (and "
":class:`~ABQflow.core.abaqus_automation.BatchAbaqusProcessor`'s "
"``run_preparation``/``run_simulation``/``run_extraction``) can invoke a "
"single phase without running the rest of the pipeline. The external "
"contract of ``execute()`` — return-dict shape and terminal-status "
"semantics — is unchanged by this split."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy:18 of
msgid "preparation_strategy"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy:-1 of
msgid "PreparationStrategy"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy:19 of
msgid "Strategy that produces the INP file."
msgstr ""

