msgid "Optional user-subroutine compile step, run before preparation."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.prepare_only:1 of
msgid "Phase 1: optional subroutine compile, preparation, optional preflight."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.prepare_only:3 of
msgid ""
"Standalone entry point for \"produce an INP (and compiled subroutine) "
"only\". Does not run pre-extraction, the solver, or post-extraction — "
"those live in :meth:`simulate_only` / :meth:`extract_only`."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.extract_only:10
#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.prepare_only:10 of
msgid "tuple[dict, JobStatusManager]"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.prepare_only:11 of
msgid ""
"``(results, status_manager)`` — *results* has at least ``'status'`` and "
"``'_phase_history'`` (plus ``'error'`` on failure), all stamped by "
":meth:`~ABQflow.core.status.JobStatusManager.finalize_into`; the manager "
"is returned so :meth:`execute` can thread it into the next phase."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.simulate_only:1 of
msgid "Phase 2: pre-extraction hooks, then the solver run."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.simulate_only:3 of
msgid ""
"Assumes ``ctx.inp_path`` already exists (produced by a prior "
":meth:`prepare_only` call — possibly in an earlier process/session, e.g. "
"via ``BatchAbaqusProcessor.run_simulation()``). Mirrors the original "
"monolithic behavior: a pre-extraction failure does *not* stop the solver "
"from running, but a solver failure does stop the pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.simulate_only:12 of
msgid "tuple[dict, JobStatusManager, bool]"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.simulate_only:13 of
msgid ""
"``(results, status_manager, stop)`` — *stop* is ``True`` when the caller "
"(e.g. :meth:`execute`) should not proceed to :meth:`extract_only` (INP "
"missing or solver failed)."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.extract_only:1 of
msgid "Phase 3: post-extraction hooks only."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.extract_only:3 of
msgid ""
"Assumes ``ctx.odb_path`` already exists. No existence guard is needed — "
":class:`OdbExtractionStrategy` already reports every task as ``None`` "
"when the ODB is missing, and :meth:`JobStatusManager.record_extraction` "
"already turns that into ``EXTRACTION_FAILED``."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.extract_only:11 of
msgid "``(results, status_manager)``."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.execute:1 of
msgid "Run the full modular workflow by composing the three phase methods."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.strategies.ModularWorkflowStrategy.execute:3 of
msgid ""
"Returns a dict with at least a ``'status'`` key plus any results from "
"pre- and post-extraction hooks.  Failing early means later phases are "
"skipped — return-dict shape and terminal-status semantics are unchanged "
"from before the phase-separation refactor."
msgstr ""

